Composery password-auth lifecycle. First boot has no password: register (or the cloud authorize flow) creates it, change-password changes it, and the server treats the no-password state as unauthenticated instead of refusing to start. login renders through the shared auth shell (renderAuthPage) with redirect-style errors and per-source rate limiting; env passwords stay mutually exclusive; the generated-password default config is gone (register owns creation). Deletes upstream's standalone login/error pages - the overlay auth shell replaces them (error.html/global.css are re-provided by the overlay).

